<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franco-Savoyard War (1600–1601)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1600">1600</a>–<a href="/years/1601">1601</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Franco-Savoyard War of 1600–1601 was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france">Henry IV of France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-emmanuel-i-duke-of-savoy">Charles Emmanuel I, Duke of Savoy</a>, over the Marquisate of Saluzzo, which Savoy had seized in 1588. French armies quickly overran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bresse">Bresse</a> and Savoy. By the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a> of 1601 the duke kept Saluzzo but ceded Bresse, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugey">Bugey</a>, Valromey and Gex to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franco-savoyard-war-1600-1601.jpg" alt="Franco-Savoyard War (1600–1601)" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonyme (1er quart 17e siècle) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henri_IV_et_la_guerre_de_Savoie.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
